D-DMRR158&#x0003e;3.0.CO;2-R</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dyck</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Zimmerman</surname><given-names>BR</given-names></name><name><surname>Vilen</surname><given-names>TH</given-names></name><name><surname>Minnerath</surname><given-names>SR</given-names></name><name><surname>Karnes</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name><name><surname>Yao</surname><given-names>JK</given-names></name><name><surname>Poduslo</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Nerve glucose, fructose, sorbitol, myo-inositol, and fiber degeneration and regeneration in diabetic neuropathy</article-title><source>N Engl J Med</source><year>1988</year><volume>319</volume><fpage>542</fpage><lpage>548</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3136330</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Biessels</surname><given-names>GJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Cristino</surname><given-names>NA</given-names></name><name><surname>Rutten</surname><given-names>GJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Hamers</surname><given-names>FP</given-names></name><name><surname>Erkelens</surname><given-names>DW</given-names></name><name><surname>Gispen</surname><given-names>WH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Neurophysiological changes in the central and peripheral nervous system of streptozotocin-diabetic rats</article-title><source>Brain</source><year>1999</year><volume>122</volume><fpage>757</fpage><lpage>768</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10219786</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/brain/122.4.757</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Leonelli</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Bianchi</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Cavaletti</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Caruso</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Crippa</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Garcia-Segura</surname><given-names>LM</given-names></name><name><surname>Lauria</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Magnaghi</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Roglio</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Melcangi</surname><given-names>RC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Progesterone and its derivatives are neuroprotective agents in experimental diabetic neuropathy: A multimodal analysis</article-title><source>Neuroscience</source><year>2007</year><volume>144</volume><fpage>1293</fpage><lpage>1304</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17187935</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.neuroscience.2006.11.014</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Vincent</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Russell</surname><given-names>JW</given-names></name><name><surname>Low</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Feldman</surname><given-names>EL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Oxidative stress in the pathogenesis of diabetic neuropathy</article-title><source>Endocr Rev</source><year>2004</year><volume>25</volume><fpage>612</fpage><lpage>628</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15294884</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1210/er.2003-0019</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tesfaye</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Chaturvedi</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Eaton</surname><given-names>SE</given-names></name><name><surname>Ward</surname><given-names>JD</given-names></name><name><sur